WEBVTT

00:01:21.563 --> 00:01:22.563
<v><b>Carla:</b></v> What’s the matter?

00:01:24.182 --> 00:01:26.963
<v><b>Emma:</b></v> Ben has another one of Izzy’s work events tonight.

00:01:29.786 --> 00:01:32.057
<v><b>Carla:</b></v> And that’s a bad thing?

00:01:32.656 --> 00:01:33.979
<v><b>Ben:</b></v> This is what it’s like:

00:01:34.875 --> 00:01:36.625
Nice to meet you, Ben.

00:01:37.203 --> 00:01:38.458
You work in a café?

00:01:38.723 --> 00:01:40.197
Aw, you’re so lucky.

00:01:40.198 --> 00:01:41.557
I love coffee.

00:01:41.745 --> 00:01:43.545
People always need coffee.

00:01:43.656 --> 00:01:44.671
Neh, neh, neh, neh, neh.

00:01:44.672 --> 00:01:45.740
Ha ha ha.

00:01:47.724 --> 00:01:48.400
<v><b>Carla:</b></v> Really?

00:01:48.958 --> 00:01:49.958
Are they all like that?

00:01:50.638 --> 00:01:53.802
<v><b>Emma:</b></v> But that’s not the real problem, is it Ben?

00:01:54.417 --> 00:01:55.808
<v><b>Ben:</b></v> No, it isn’t.

00:01:57.203 --> 00:01:57.818
It’s Izzy.

00:01:58.557 --> 00:02:01.343
She’s different when she’s with the people from work.

00:02:02.495 --> 00:02:03.947
<v><b>Carla:</b></v> Well, she’s working.

00:02:04.561 --> 00:02:06.494
We’re all different at work, aren’t we?

00:02:08.911 --> 00:02:10.276
Hi, can I help you?

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.104
Hi, can I help you?

00:02:12.292 --> 00:02:13.750
To have here or take away?

00:02:14.092 --> 00:02:14.999
Thanks very much.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:15.984
Have a nice day!

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.724
<v><b>Emma:</b></v> Well, I’m not different at work.

00:02:18.375 --> 00:02:19.531
<v><b>Carla:</b></v> You work on a farm!

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:22.131
You spend most of your time talking to animals!

00:02:25.271 --> 00:02:27.141
<v><b>Ben:</b></v> I know it’s because she’s at work,

00:02:27.552 --> 00:02:29.698
but…she’s always at work.

00:02:30.422 --> 00:02:35.943
I don’t want to spend all our free time with her work friends, especially Max.

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:41.338
<v><b>Carla:</b></v> Well, I’m sure you’re going somewhere really nice this evening.

00:02:42.193 --> 00:02:43.052
<v><b>Ben:</b></v> ‘This evening’

00:02:43.193 --> 00:02:47.891
I would just like to have a pizza with my girlfriend on the sofa in her apartment.

00:02:48.182 --> 00:02:51.896
I don’t want to have to dress up and go out to a nice restaurant.

00:02:52.135 --> 00:02:53.708
I want it to be like before.

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:55.584
I want Izzy back!

00:02:58.375 --> 00:02:59.609
<v><b>Carla:</b></v> Izzy is still here.

00:03:00.484 --> 00:03:01.250
<v><b>Emma:</b></v> Is she…?

00:03:06.406 --> 00:03:07.073
<v><b>Ben:</b></v> I don’t know.